      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly! When a user submits a formal \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR, a company must follow these mandatory steps, with a touch of our little mischievous gnome friends in mind:\n\n1. **Receive the Request**: The user sends a formal request to the company, much like a goblin sending a raven with a message. The company must acknowledge receipt promptly.\n\n2. **Verify Identity**: Before proceeding, the company must verify the identity of the user, akin to a goblin proving its lineage to a royal court.\n\n3. **Assess the Request**: The company must assess whether the request is valid and falls under GDPR's scope, just as a wise old goblin would ponder over a tricky riddle.\n\n4. **Determine Data to Delete**: Identify all personal data related to the user, much like a goblin would gather all its trinkets and treasures.\n\n5. **Delete the Data**: Erase the identified data from all systems and backups, ensuring no trace remains, just as a goblin would cover its tracks after a midnight heist.\n\n6. **Notify Third Parties**: Inform any third parties that hold the data, similar to a goblin informing its allies of a secret",
      "source": "target",
