    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I apologize for the confusion. Here is a revised, professional summary of the mandatory steps a company must follow when a user submits a formal \"right to be forgotten\" request under GDPR:\n\n1. **Acknowledge Receipt**: The company must acknowledge the receipt of the request within one month of receipt, as per GDPR Article 12(5).\n\n2. **Verify Identity**: The company must verify the identity of the data subject to ensure the request is legitimate.\n\n3. **Assess the Request**: The company must assess whether the request meets the criteria for the right to be forgotten, including whether the data is no longer necessary for the purposes it was collected for or processed.\n\n4. **Determine Data to Delete**: The company must identify all personal data related to the user, including any copies held by third parties.\n\n5. **Delete the Data**: The company must delete the identified personal data from all systems and backups, ensuring no trace remains.\n\n6. **Notify Third Parties**: If the data is held by third parties, the company must inform them of the request and ensure they comply with the deletion.\n\n7. **Document the Process**: The company must document the process and outcome of the request, including any challenges faced",
